// Behavioral fixture — Proposal B: lay down ALL combos via a stage loop.
//
// `until Set in Hand empty` is a valid end condition: `Set in Hand` is a
// cardset (a combo group), and `card_set_empty` works on any cardset. The
// stage re-prompts each iteration until no combo-matching cards remain.
//
// Deck: Ace, Ace, Ace, Two, Two (one suit). The player lays down the three
// Aces in iteration 1; the loop-back check then finds the two Twos no longer
// match ("same Rank and size >= 3" needs >= 3 cards) -> stage exits.
player P1
turnorder (P:P1)
location Hand on P:P1
location Table on table
location Deck on table

combo Set where (same Rank and size >= 3)

card on Deck:
  Rank(Ace, Ace, Ace, Two, Two)
    for Suit(Diamonds)

stage Deal for current 1 times {
  deal 5 from Deck private to Hand
}

stage Laydown for current until Set in Hand empty {
  move Set in Hand of current private to Table
}
